# Suite psg: the PSG register file, then (plans 05-05..05-08) the ports, tone, mixer, noise, envelope,
# sample stream and write log (AUD-01, plan 05-04, A-12).
# Plan 05-04: one id per vector of data/psg/vectors/regs.txt (psg.reg.*, 28) and reset.txt (psg.reset.*, 2),
# evaluated through the memory-system bus against the register-address literal; the register-map,
# reset, bus, no-mirror, purity and guest tests; and the two judge self-controls (psg.judge.*).
# Plan 05-05: the port family (data/psg/vectors/port.txt, psg.port.*, 10), evaluated through the bus READ with
# the pins of the vector's pin key and the direction bits of R7, and its judge self-control.
# Plan 05-06: the engine families tone (tone.txt, psg.tone.*, 16 plus the guest tracer), mix (mix.txt, 10) and amp
# (amp.txt, 6), judged on the sample stream or the pure functions by psg_tone.c and psg_mix.c, and two judge
# self-controls (psg.judge.tone-row-changed, psg.judge.mix-row-changed).
# Plan 05-06 (Task 3): the bounds derived from the CPU model (psg.bounds.*, 5) and the audio buffer rules of the public
# run call with a guest that makes sound (psg.buffers.*, 6).
# Plan 05-08: the published write-log bounds (psg.bounds.g-and-u, log-capacity-formula, log-bound-at-g), the write-log
# buffer rules (psg.buffers.worst-case-writer, log-too-small, log-not-requested, log-sentinel-tail, log-safety-net)
# and the write-log family psg.log.* (framing, window, vs-cpu-trace, replay, effect boundary, bytes), psg.slice.log-*,
# the eight seeded fuzz cases psg.fuzz.seed01..08, psg.iso.interleaved-instances and psg.reset.*-cleared.
# The vector families wired into the suite are the ones NOT listed in data/psg/vectors-pending.ids.
